Title: python.vim
Author: Rich Cheng
Purpose: Python file type configuration
Language: Vimscript

@ This file, installed at |.vim/after/ftplugins/python.vim| contains my Python
filetype specific configuration.

@heading Tab Settings per PEP 8.
We're going to let tabs display as the standard 8 characters, and use
|'shiftwidth'| and |'expandtab'| to indent by 4 spaces.

|'smarttab'| is also set so that |<BS>| at the start of a line removes
spaces.

We could also have achieved this by setting |'softtabstop'| to a negative value:
The difference between the two occurs when you press |<Tab>| and you're NOT
at the start of a line:

(*) with |set smarttab|, |<Tab>| will jump to the next |'tabstop'|
(*) with |set softtabstop=-1|, |<Tab>| will jump to the next |'shiftwidth'|
=
setlocal tabstop& shiftwidth=4 softtabstop=0 smarttab expandtab

@ We also set |'list'| so any errant |<Tab>| characters that DO make it into
the file are easily spotted.
=
setlocal list

@heading Auto formatting.

(*) c - automatic formatting of comments (using the |'textwidth'| setting
below)
(*) q - Allow formatting comments with |gq|
(*) j - remove comment leaders when joining lines
(*) r - add comment leader when pressing |<Enter>|

See |:help fo-table| for further details.
=
setlocal formatoptions=cqjr
setlocal textwidth=79

@heading PEP 8 Line Length. We set |'colorcolumn'| to 80: any lines touching
the line are over the PEP 8 recommendation.
=
setlocal colorcolumn=80

@heading Set up 'makeprg' and 'errorformat'.
FIXME
=
compiler flake8

@heading Use my indent foldexpr.
FIXME
=
let g:include_blanks_in_fold_above = 1
set foldexpr=alternate_indent_foldexpr#foldlevel(v:lnum)
set foldmethod=expr

@heading Load the PEP 8 indenting script.
=
if has('packages')
  packadd vim-python-pep8-indent
endif
